{{!-- The tab rail, shared by the NPC and item sheets. Its own render part, so the set of tabs can
      change without rebuilding the tab bodies beneath it.

      The two rules are DRAWN, like every other rule in the system — the strip used to sit between
      two CSS borders, and a machined line a few pixels from the window's drawn frame reads as a
      seam between two designs. The rail and its rules are one element for the same reason the
      character sheet's strip is: a part's template is a single element, and the rules belong to
      the strip rather than floating between parts. --}}
<div class="cairn-nav-block">
    <div class="cairn-tab-rule" data-ink="hline" data-ink-seed="nav-rule-over" data-ink-w="1.8"></div>
    <nav class="tabs cairn-tab-rail" data-group="primary">
        {{#each tabs as |tab|}}
        <a class="cairn-tab {{tab.cssClass}}" data-action="tab" data-group="primary" data-tab="{{tab.id}}">
            {{localize tab.label}}
        </a>
        {{/each}}
    </nav>
    <div class="cairn-tab-rule" data-ink="hline" data-ink-seed="nav-rule-under" data-ink-w="1.8"></div>
</div>
